\name{cellucid_field_group}
\alias{cellucid_field_group}
\title{Group categories into a new field}
\usage{
cellucid_field_group(viewer, field, groups, name, rest = NULL)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{The categorical column whose categories are grouped. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The column name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{Exactly \code{"obs"}. Required.}}}
\item{groups}{The new categories, in order, each with the categories it holds (a category in one group at most). A vector or list of a named list (at least 1 item). Required.}
\item{name}{The new column's name; by default "<name> (grouped)", numbered when taken. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{rest}{The category every category no group lists joins ("Other", or a group's label); null keeps each as it is. Text or \code{NULL} (at least 1 character). Default \code{NULL}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
A new categorical column from another, whose categories are groups of its categories (a lineage from cell types: Ductal and Ngn3 low EP as "Progenitor", Alpha, Beta, Delta and Epsilon as "Endocrine"), shown at once; the column it is made from stays. A category no group lists is kept as it is, or joins rest when rest names a category. One step: one undo.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{field.group} (Fields). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{field-overlays}, \code{active-field}, \code{colors}, \code{filters}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_field_group(viewer, field = list(key = "cell_type",
      source = "obs"), groups = list(list(categories = c("Ductal",
      "Ngn3 low EP"), label = "Progenitor"), list(categories = c("Alpha",
      "Beta"), label = "Endocrine")))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
